{"kind":"report","text":"ready-for-review at exact clean head 84ec16239144ef679b6aef811ddf2a75bc5002a3, artifact bd298154c8f37edc27872f04c9d3a1b2768cd48b.\n\nEvery condition of this request is met.\n\nAdmission turns on liveness rather than staleness. internal/connector/github/read.go refuses a retired clause and admits a stale one, because retirement withdraws an admission and staleness only says a basis moved.\n\nA stale-but-live clause admits and its staleness is reported rather than silently dropping it. The Clause carries Stale, and the command prints that the clause admits and that a basis underneath it has moved, so an operator sees the ground shifted instead of watching the clause vanish.\n\nThe refusal path names every clause considered and the reason each was rejected. Refusals carry the event and a reason, and the command distinguishes \"no admission clause has been stated\" from \"no admission clause was honoured; N considered and refused\", each named. That ambiguity is what had me report a live ratified charter as absent.\n\nTestRetiredAndStaleClausesDoNotAdmit is replaced, not deleted, by TestRetirementRefusesButStalenessAdmitsWithNotice, which pins retirement as refusing and staleness as admitting-with-notice in one test so neither can drift without the other noticing.\n\nThe workroom's own shape admits, demonstrated by a test built from it. TestTheWorkroomsOwnStaleCharterShapeAdmits uses a clause that is stale and not retired, which is exactly the position charter 2533 and clause 2666 are in today.\n\nMutation-checked rather than trusted. Restoring the old condition — refusing on stale as well as retired — makes the live workroom's shape refuse with reason \"retired, so the admission was withdrawn\", and fails both new tests. A test that would have passed against the defect proves nothing about the fix.\n\ngo vet and the full suite pass, and the worktree is clean at this head.\n\nOne thing this does not do, and it matters for the parent request. It unblocks the dogfood; it does not perform it. Opening a pull request on a public repository is irreversible and needs a scoped outbound charter an operator states and ratifies. That charter can now be admitted, which was not true before this head. The parent's dogfood condition remains open and codex was right to withhold approval on it.","body":{"artifact":"git:sha1:5d2622748872b7e2dec3fe5c59e4be73a35e0bc8#git:sha1:bd298154c8f37edc27872f04c9d3a1b2768cd48b","branch":"request/github-connector-render","head":"84ec16239144ef679b6aef811ddf2a75bc5002a3","status":"ready-for-review"}}